"Places defined risk scenarios on likelihood and consequence bands to guide discussion and response priorities.\n\nUse when: Screen operational risks using a shared assessment convention. Compare initial and residual exposure after proposed controls.\n\nAvoid when: Exact expected loss or a reliable ranking within broad risk bands is required.\n\nVisual grammar: Axes encode explicitly defined likelihood and consequence scales. Cells show risk bands under a stated organizational policy. Risk identifiers locate scenarios without replacing their full descriptions.\n\nBuild: Define scenarios as cause, uncertain event and consequence. Calibrate axis bands and the assessment period. Place risks using evidence and record owners, controls and uncertainty separately.\n\nCheck: Likelihood and consequence refer to the same scenario and horizon. Ordinal categories are not treated as precise arithmetic measurements. Initial and residual assessments are clearly distinguished.\n\nPitfalls: Multiplying arbitrary category numbers as if they were physical quantities. Calling a low-frequency catastrophic event harmless because of its color.\n\nExample: A warehouse reviews equipment failure scenarios, placing each by annual likelihood and credible consequence before assigning response owners.\n\nAlternatives: Bow-tie diagram, Risk breakdown structure."
